diff --git a/docs/figma/inventory-assets.md b/docs/figma/inventory-assets.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..b937ded
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/figma/inventory-assets.md
@@ -0,0 +1,117 @@
+# Inventory panel image assets
+
+These are the parts of the Figma inventory panel (`design/figma/inventory-panel.json`, screen
+`12:340`, Slot component set `20:1`) that the Roblox build draws as uploaded images, because Roblox
+UI objects can't draw them. Everything else is built from UI objects (see the end of this page).
+
+The code reads every asset id from `InventoryStyle.Asset` in
+`src/StarterPlayer/StarterPlayerScripts/UI/InventoryStyle.luau`. They are all
+`rbxassetid://0` for now. Until an id is filled in, the code draws a stand-in: a rounded square in
+the block's color for block art, a text glyph for the icons, and nothing for the shadow, glow and
+pattern.
+
+## Export rules
+
+- **Export at 2x.** The UI is laid out in 1080p pixels (the Figma pixel sizes) and `Screen.luau`
+  scales it up to 2x on 4K screens, so 2x images stay sharp everywhere. The "Draw size" column
+  below is the size in Figma / 1080p pixels; the "Export size" column is the PNG size.
+- **PNG with transparency**, nothing outside the stated frame.
+- **White on transparent** for anything marked "tinted". The code sets the color with
+  `ImageColor3` and the opacity with `ImageTransparency`, so export these at 100% opacity, not with
+  the Figma color or opacity applied.
+- Keep every image at or under 1024 px on each side; Roblox downscales larger uploads.
+
+## Assets
+
+| `InventoryStyle.Asset` key | What it is (Figma node) | Draw size | Export size | How it's drawn in Roblox |
+|---|---|---|---|---|
+| `PanelShadow` | Panel drop shadow (`40:88` effect: black 45%, y 12, blur 32) | 9-slice, stretched to panel + 32 px per side | 320 x 320 | `ImageLabel`, `ScaleType.Slice`, `SliceCenter = Rect(96, 96, 224, 224)`, `SliceScale = 0.5`, size `(1, 64, 1, 64)`, centered on the panel and moved down 12. Tinted black, `ImageTransparency = 0.55`. Sits behind the panel background. |
+| `HexPattern` | Hex Pattern group (`40:78`): 41 outlined hexagons at 6% | Tile of 112 x 192 | 224 x 384 | `ImageLabel`, `ScaleType.Tile`, `TileSize = 112 x 192`, starting at (-56, -16) from the panel's top-left and covering the panel. Tinted white, `ImageTransparency = 0.94`. Inside a `CanvasGroup` with a 16 px `UICorner` so it's clipped to the panel's rounded corners. |
+| `SlotGlow` | Selected slot glow (`20:3` effect: accent 55%, blur 16, spread 2) | 136 x 136 | 272 x 272 | `ImageLabel` centered behind the selected slot, shown only for the selected slot. Tinted accent `#FFC83C`, `ImageTransparency = 0.45`. |
+| `CloseIcon` | Icon/Close (`40:80`) | 20 x 20 | 40 x 40 | `ImageLabel`, `ScaleType.Fit`, centered in the 44 x 44 close button. Tinted Text/Primary `#F5F6FA`. |
+| `LockIcon` | Icon/Lock (`40:30`, `40:100`) | 24 x 24 | 48 x 48 | `ImageLabel`, `ScaleType.Fit`, at (36, 26) in a locked slot. Tinted Text/Primary `#F5F6FA`. |
+| `BlockArt.Brick` | Block Art in Slot / Brick (`40:0`) | 72 x 72 | 144 x 144 | See "Block art" below. |
+| `BlockArt.Dirt` | Block Art in Slot / Dirt (`40:4`) | 72 x 72 | 144 x 144 | 〃 |
+| `BlockArt.Grass` | Block Art in Slot / Grass (`40:8`) | 72 x 72 | 144 x 144 | 〃 |
+| `BlockArt.Window` | Block Art in Slot / Window (`40:12`) | 72 x 72 | 144 x 144 | 〃 |
+| `BlockArt.Wood` | Block Art in Slot / Wood (`40:16`) | 72 x 72 | 144 x 144 | 〃 |
+| `BlockArt.Stone` | Block Art in Slot / Stone (`40:20`) | 72 x 72 | 144 x 144 | 〃 |
+| `BlockArt.Sand` | Block Art in Slot / Sand (`40:24`) | 72 x 72 | 144 x 144 | 〃 |
+| `BlockArt.Ice` | Block Art in Slot / Ice (`40:28`) | 72 x 72 | 144 x 144 | 〃 |
+| `BlockArt.Lamp` | Block Art in Slot / Lamp (`40:33`) | 72 x 72 | 144 x 144 | 〃 |
+| `BlockArt.Gold` | Block Art in Slot / Gold (`40:38`) | 72 x 72 | 144 x 144 | 〃 |
+
+## How to build each export in Figma
+
+### Panel shadow
+
+1. Make a 160 x 160 frame with no fill and clipping off.
+2. Inside it, at (32, 32), draw a 96 x 96 rectangle with corner radius 16 and a **white** fill.
+3. Give the rectangle a drop shadow: white, 100%, x 0, y 0, blur 32, spread 0 (the y offset of
+   12 and the 45% opacity are applied in Roblox).
+4. Export the frame at 2x (320 x 320).
+
+The corners of the 9-slice are 48 px at 1x (32 px of blur plus the 16 px corner), which is what
+`SliceCenter` cuts at. The white rectangle in the middle is hidden under the panel, so it doesn't
+matter that it's opaque.
+
+### Hex pattern tile
+
+The hexagons are pointy-top, 112 x 128, spaced 112 across and 96 down, with every other row
+shifted 56 to the right, so the pattern repeats every 112 x 192.
+
+1. Copy enough of the Hex Pattern group to cover at least 3 x 3 hexagons, with the strokes
+   **white, 100%, 2 px, centered** (the group's 6% opacity is applied in Roblox).
+2. Put a 112 x 192 frame with **clip content on** over it, with its top-left corner exactly on the
+   top-left of the bounding box of a hexagon in an unshifted row.
+3. Export the frame at 2x (224 x 384). Check it tiles without seams by placing two copies side by
+   side and two stacked.
+
+### Selected slot glow
+
+1. Make a 136 x 136 frame with no fill and clipping off.
+2. Inside it, at (20, 20), draw a 96 x 96 rectangle with corner radius 12 and a **white** fill.
+3. Give the rectangle a drop shadow: white, 100%, x 0, y 0, blur 16, spread 2.
+4. Export the frame at 2x (272 x 272).
+
+The slot covers the middle, so the opaque rectangle never shows.
+
+### Icons
+
+Export Icon/Close and Icon/Lock on their own, **white**, at 2x: 40 x 40 and 48 x 48. Keep the
+icon's own padding inside the 20 x 20 or 24 x 24 bounds as it is in Figma.
+
+### Block art
+
+The art in each slot is an image fill (scale mode Fit) on a 56 x 56 rectangle with a drop shadow
+(black 40%, y 4, blur 8). Roblox can't put a shadow on an image, so the shadow is baked into the
+export:
+
+1. Make a 72 x 72 frame with no fill and clipping off.
+2. Put the slot's Block Art rectangle inside it at (8, 4), keeping its drop shadow as it is in
+   Figma (black 40%, y 4, blur 8).
+3. Export the frame at 2x (144 x 144).
+
+Use the same frame and position for all ten blocks so they line up. In Roblox the image is a
+72 x 72 `ImageLabel` at (12, 12) in the slot, which puts the 56 x 56 art at (20, 16) as in
+Figma. Locked slots set `ImageTransparency = 0.6`, the Figma Content frame's 40% opacity.
+
+## Not images: what's built from UI objects
+
+| Figma | Roblox |
+|---|---|
+| Panel fill `#171A26` at 92%, 16 px corners | `Frame`, `BackgroundTransparency = 0.08`, `UICorner` |
+| Panel 2 px inside stroke `#3A4060` | `UIStroke`, `BorderStrokePosition.Inner` |
+| Slot vertical gradient `#2B3150` to `#20253B`, 12 px corners | `UIGradient` (rotation 90), `UICorner` |
+| Slot stroke: 1 px inside `#3A4060`; Selected: 3 px outside `#FFC83C` | `UIStroke`, `Inner` or `Outer` |
+| Close button: white 8% circle | `TextButton`, `BackgroundTransparency = 0.92`, `UICorner(0.5, 0)` |
+| Equip button gradient `#FFD25A` to `#FF9F1C` with a 3 px inner shadow along the bottom | A `TextButton` in the shaded color (`#BF7715`) with a gradient face 3 px shorter on top |
+| Text drop shadows (title y 2, count y 1) | A black copy of the label behind it, offset by the shadow's y. The count's 2 px blur is dropped. |
+| All text, Builder Sans Medium / Bold / ExtraBold | `TextLabel` with `Font.new("rbxasset://fonts/families/BuilderSans.json", weight)` |
+
+### Left out
+
+- **Background blur (24) behind the panel.** Roblox can only blur the whole 3D view (a
+  `BlurEffect` in Lighting), not what's behind one GUI object, so the panel is just the 92% fill.
+- **Title letter spacing (+2 px).** Roblox text has no letter-spacing setting; the title is
+  about 16 px narrower than in Figma.
diff --git a/src/StarterPlayer/StarterPlayerScripts/Main.client.luau b/src/StarterPlayer/StarterPlayerScripts/Main.client.luau
index daf599e..addda50 100644
